raphael: Redmi K20 Pro / Mi 9T Pro (SM8150) board, volume-up key, GT9886 touch

sweet_board.h gains sweet_board_raphael() (ADT root compatible
"xiaomi,raphael"; the ADT keeps "xiaomi,sweet" too, so every other driver
takes the sweet defaults, which already ran on raphael with xnu-8796).

sweet_keys.c: volume-up is PM8150 GPIO6 at SPMI SID 0 0xc500 (status
0xc510), the same peripheral address as on the Poco F1.

sweet_touch.c: a third touch board. Goodix GT9886 (Normandy protocol) at
0x5d on QUP19 = wrapper 2 SE2 @0xc88000, SDA/SCL GPIO 57/58 function 2,
reset 54, IRQ 122, load switches GPIO 98/100, all in the TLMM SOUTH tile
(0x03d00000). Clocks: GCC vote 0x52014 bits 1/2/6, RCG 0x1e3a8, wrapper 2
AHB branches 0x1e004/0x1e008 (the latter hardware gated); a DFS RCG uses the
first boot-programmed XO/1 level through the SE CLK_SEL. The clocks are
voted before the first SE register read. Protocol from Xiaomi raphael-p-oss
goodix_driver_gt9886 + goodix_gt9886_cfg_f11.bin: doze off via
0x30f0/0x3100, 72-byte version block at 0x452c (zero sum, PID "9886",
sensor ID 0x4541), frames at 0x4100 with an 8-bit zero-sum checksum and a
0x00 acknowledge; sensor 0 mirrors both axes, sweettouchflip=N overrides.
Ported from UniXNU-raphael patch 0112 (xnu-8796, verified on the phone
2026-11-05). A GSI-only SE falls back to the existing bit-banged I2C.
The sweet and beryllium boards are unchanged (their new table fields are 0).

Host test: tools/raphael/touch-test (109 checks).

